<id/14/1402/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Felspar"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_industrial_minerals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a silicious mineral, of which there are several varieties, displaying elegant and varied iridescent colours. Cornish stone or porcelain clay is one of the products of decomposed felspar. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 162]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_industrial_minerals): Named mineral (slates, felspar, barytes, kieselguhr) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 12 rows, 1893–1901. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×9. Units: Tons ×12. Top routes: Canada → United States ×3; Canada → All Countries ×3; Ontario → All Countries ×3; Canada → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1402" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Felspar"@en ;
